{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_55372fbba2cc15e76ccafba155793f47c06fc732ecb8f590b25ab0a45e196324", "title": "Shorty Medlocke", "text": "Shorty Medlocke (born Paul Robert Medlock, 1910 – 1982) was an American delta blues and hard rock musician and banjo player. He is the grandfather of Rickey Medlocke of the Southern rock band Blackfoot. His surname was originally spelled without an \"e\" on the end.", "score": 31.3955}, {"id": "hp_doc_ed8ae355818bf00f7be7eb3f1e3338d14808ef39262ac237abf4cb2a85159c46", "title": "Rickey Medlocke", "text": "Rickey Medlocke (born February 17, 1950) is an American musician best known as the frontman/guitarist for the southern rock band Blackfoot and a member of Lynyrd Skynyrd. During his first stint with Lynyrd Skynyrd from 1971-1972 he played drums and sang lead on a few songs that would initially be released on 1978's \"First and Last\". Medlocke would rejoin Blackfoot in 1972 and later returned to Lynyrd Skynyrd in 1996 as a guitarist with whom he continues to tour and record today.", "score": 28.1745}, {"id": "hp_doc_2fbddeeb89bf98d7b228c16e8457ca81cd0a1061d9866dbf1675cc681df38fab", "title": "Blackfoot (band)", "text": "Blackfoot is an American Southern rock band from Jacksonville, Florida formed during 1970. Though they primarily play with a Southern rock style, they are also known as a hard rock act. The band's classic lineup consisted of guitarist and vocalist Rickey Medlocke, guitarist Charlie Hargrett, bassist Greg T. Walker, and drummer Jakson Spires.", "score": 28.0569}], "remaining_searches": 2}
